course: dictionary
lesson: 11888
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Brew can mean a drink, a magic mixture, or something that is about to happen. The words around it are the clues.
explain: «Dad, can you put a brew on?» In the UK, a brew is an informal word for a cup of tea. «Grandma brewed a pot of tea for us» shows the verb meaning: to make a drink by mixing it with hot water.
explain: «Dark clouds are brewing over the hills.» Clouds cannot make a cup of tea, so brewing here means something is slowly getting ready to happen. Bad weather is coming.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence. Then put your meaning in place of the hard word and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Brew can be a verb (to brew) or a noun (a brew).
fact: «Brew» means to make tea or coffee by mixing it with hot water.
fact: «Brew» can also mean to make beer by soaking, boiling and fermenting grain.
fact: «Trouble is brewing» means trouble is about to happen.
fact: In science, brewing uses yeast to turn sugar into alcohol and gas.
exercise: «Dad, can you put a brew on?» What does a brew mean here? | A witch's magic potion | *A cup of tea | A storm about to start | A heavy bag
exercise: «Dark clouds are brewing over the hills.» What does brewing mean? | Making a cup of tea | *Slowly getting ready to happen | Shining brightly | Falling down the hill
exercise: «The witch stirred a strange brew in her cauldron.» What is the brew? | A cup of tea for guests | A loud noise | A bird's nest | *A mixture
test: «Trouble is brewing in the playground.» What does brewing mean? | Being made into tea | *About to start | Being washed clean | Being sold at the shop
test: «Grandad says he fancies a brew.» What does Grandad want? | A long bath | *A cup of tea | A new hat | A walk in the park
exam: In science, what does brewing use to turn sugar into alcohol and gas? | Ice | Salt | Sand | *Yeast
